  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA large area of high pressure will generally be positioned \nacross SE Canada through much of the week, before shifting \nsouth/east directly over the Northeast CONUS over the weekend. \nMeanwhile, a Nor'easter positioned off the N. Carolina coast \nwill slowly meander E/NE over the next few days with no \nimmediate impacts to eastern New York and western New England. \nThe pressure gradient is expected to tighten on Tue, so \nnortherly winds will increase with gusts of 20-25 mph \ndeveloping. Otherwise winds should remain relatively light, with\nplenty of clear skies upcoming. High temperatures will be near \nnormal, with lows averaging slightly below normal most nights \nwith a dry air mass in place. There will also likely be patchy \nfog in favored sheltered valley and near bodies of water some\nnights, especially during periods when winds will be lighter.",
